A type system technique where a variable's type can differ at each occurrence (use) based on what predicates have been checked - the same variable x can have type Number in one branch and String in another. Synonymous with ${fref("/01-programming-language-theory/02-concepts/flow-typing.td")}.

A type system technique where a variable's type can **differ at each occurrence** (use) based on what predicates have been checked - the same variable `x` can have type `Number` in one branch and `String` in another. Synonymous with Flow typing.
